and record the empirical k-th central moments of (r1 - S*I)/sqrt(S*I) in dyadic blocks.
If the tail is Gaussian/Poisson-like, an exception (r1 = 0) at N ~ X would be a deviation
of ~ sqrt(S(N) I(N)) ~ sqrt(N)/log N standard deviations: the *quantitative* target that a
moment-method proof (k-th moment of the minor-arc integral) would have to certify.
Run: python3 goldbach_moments.py [LIMIT]
